  "result": "I've written the 30-minute lesson on O3 (context and memory), a five-item quiz with its answer key, and a one-page cheat sheet. I couldn't run a word count (the shell command needed approval), so I haven't checked the length against 30 minutes.\n\n**Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`. Every example is the makerspace assistant.\n- **Context window and cost:** the model keeps nothing between calls, the whole context is re-sent and paid for on every step, and recall gets worse as the window fills (Anthropic calls this context rot).\n- **Between steps:** the context only grows during a request. Keep tool results small and clear the ones already used.\n- **Between sessions:** only what your program saves survives. The lesson covers what to write as notes and what to look up fresh, and why a saved copy of live calendar data goes stale.\n- **Retrieval:** splitting the manuals into chunks and indexing them, a `search_manuals` tool, and the two ways it can fail (wrong chunk returned, or right chunk misread).\n- **Practice:** a warm-up recall question on the agent loop, three check-yourself questions, a worked example with an illustrative token count, and a faded practice task.\n- **Primary source:** Anthropic's \"Effective context engineering for AI agents\". The sources I used are also recorded in `RESOURCES.md`.\n\n**Quiz:** quiz 0002 is ready when you are. The answers are in `keys/0002.json`.\n\n**Also written:**\n- `cheatsheets/context-and-memory.html`\n- a shared stylesheet, `assets/lesson.css`, so later lessons look alike\n- a line in `NOTES.md` recording the lesson and quiz\n\n**Open questions for you:**\n- Do you want the quiz in the chat now?\n- Quiz 0001 is still ungraded, with two submissions (`submissions/s1.json` and `s2.json`). Should I grade both next?",
